**Why I stopped instead of auto-publishing.** verify-claims checked the brief's facts against the live pleasur.ai pricing page and found **two false premises about our own product** that the earlier gates had trusted from the brief:

1. **No $19/mo plan exists.** Real tiers: Starter $12.99/mo ($5.20 annual), Standard $27.99 ($11.20), Ultimate $49.99 ($20.00). On annual, **pleasur.ai is cheaper** than Secrets AI's $13.33 — the article's "concede price, counter on value" thesis is backwards.
2. **The `[GAIN]` differentiator is false.** The article's reason-to-exist was "pleasur.ai has no credit metering vs Secrets AI's Moments." But pleasur.ai also runs a coin economy (image gen 10 coins, voice 10, calls 50/min). The differentiator collapses.

(Plus genfindr reads 7.3/10 live, not the brief's 7.6.)

These invalidate the thesis, the `[GAIN]`, the table, and the pricing/FAQ sections — not a surgical fix. Misstating our own flagship's price/capabilities in published copy is the brand-risk case CLAUDE.md says to escalate, and the reframe is a positioning call the board owns.

